  "narrative": "Early-2026 data show a record-start pace with ~606 deaths by late Feb. If March maintains high fatality levels, reaching 900 before April is highly plausible, yielding a calibrated posterior near 0.99. Uncertainties remain from weather, SAR capacity, and reporting lags, but the balance strongly favors hitting the threshold."
  ,
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.92,
      "basis": "Reference class anchored to Mediterranean fatalities pace on the Central Mediterranean route; early-2026 toll is already elevated relative to historical baselines, justifying a high anchor probability."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Current pace through late February 2026",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "606 deaths by February 24 imply a sustained pace that would approach or exceed 900 by end-March if continued."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Historical base-rate for Mediterranean deaths (roughly 2,100–2,200 per year; 2025: ~2,185)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Annual mortality levels suggest that a large portion of the year's toll could occur in a short interval, making the 900 mark plausible by March."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Severe weather events increasing fatalities (e.g., storms in Jan 2026)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Weather-driven spikes have historically raised March–April tolls; ongoing adverse conditions could push March fatalities higher."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Migration policy and SAR capacity changes (tighter controls, potential reductions in rescue operations)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Less rescue capacity and stricter controls can raise fatality risk, contributing to an elevated chance of reaching 900."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Data reporting gaps and verification lags",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Underreporting or delayed data could mean uncounted deaths push the eventual tally above 900 even if current counts are lower."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Given the strongest updates come from the pace through February and weather risk, these push the posterior toward 0.99. Baseline annual mortality provides context that such a surge within a few weeks is plausible. Some downward calibrations exist due to reporting lags and potential policy changes, but the overall weighting favors crossing 900 by end-March."
  }
}

